WEBVTT

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:16.720
It's the third match of Washizu Mahjong, 
where death and ruin are the wagers.

00:01:17.390 --> 00:01:20.450
With his godly luck, Washizu 
has turned his hand into

00:01:20.450 --> 00:01:25.500
a riichi, 12-dora monster, 
a counted yakuman.

00:01:20.450 --> 00:01:25.500
Counted yakuman - Once you have 13 han 
or more, your hand is considered a yakuman.

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:27.030
Now he is about to draw 
from the dead wall.

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:32.530
<i>You are going to die, Akagi Shigeru.</i>

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:36.170
If he wins from it, he gets 
16,000 from everybody.

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:41.010
Akagi has already lost 
1,100 CCs of blood,

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:46.450
and would lose another 1,600 CCs 
for a total of 2,700 CCs,

00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:48.620
which far surpasses the lethal amount.

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:55.510
<b>Episode 25</b>

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:55.510
<b>The Temptation of Murderous Intent</b>

00:01:56.420 --> 00:02:00.960
<i>Kill! Kill! Kill! Kill! Kill!</i>

00:02:01.310 --> 00:02:03.830
<i>Come on, 1 of circles!</i>

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:13.610
Were they summoned by the madness 
of Washizu, possessed by evil?

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:21.880
Devils, demons, and evil spirits 
have come in great numbers to kill...

00:02:24.790 --> 00:02:26.890
Akagi Shigeru.

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:34.080
<i>Kill! Kill! Kill! Kill! Kill! Kill!</i>

00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:37.400
But Akagi deflects it.

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:44.910
The demons, the monsters, 
the devils, the evil, the madness!

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:52.110
<i>What is it with this brat?</i>

00:02:52.110 --> 00:02:53.850
<i>He still won't tremble?</i>

00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:55.850
<i>He still refuses to fear me?</i>

00:02:56.490 --> 00:03:00.860
<i>Me, who stands at the 
highest pinnacle of all?</i>

00:03:01.350 --> 00:03:04.860
<i>Me, Washizu Iwao, 
the incarnation of God?!</i>

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:13.530
<i>Which one was it?</i>

00:03:14.350 --> 00:03:18.270
<i>The tile I drew in before...</i>

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:20.470
<i>Is it this one?</i>

00:03:29.030 --> 00:03:29.950
No success.

00:03:29.950 --> 00:03:30.950
Damn it!

00:03:32.380 --> 00:03:34.890
Washizu's dead wall 
draw did not succeed.

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:42.350
At one point, Washizu had his 
fingers closed on the winning tile.

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:48.780
He reached for the heavens 
but couldn't grasp them.

00:03:48.780 --> 00:03:51.490
He had the chance of a lifetime, 
but let it slip away.

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:56.640
Akagi, on the other hand, survived.

00:03:57.650 --> 00:04:00.640
With that said, he's still 
just one step away from death.

00:04:01.730 --> 00:04:04.500
His desperate situation still continues.

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:08.080
<i>Washizu-sama.</i>

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:10.720
<i>Let me deal into your hand.</i>

00:04:11.780 --> 00:04:12.730
At this point,

00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:14.960
Akagi has 37,000 points.

00:04:14.960 --> 00:04:16.470
If Washizu wins this dealer yakuman

00:04:16.470 --> 00:04:18.380
with 48,000 points,

00:04:18.380 --> 00:04:20.060
he'll overtake Akagi

00:04:20.060 --> 00:04:22.540
and have a 33,000 point lead.

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:28.040
<i>With that big a lead, you should be 
able to win this East-South match.</i>

00:04:28.970 --> 00:04:31.220
<i>Let's end it here, Washizu-sama.</i>

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:37.580
<i>I suppose so.</i>

00:04:37.580 --> 00:04:42.050
<i>Anybody would think this is enough.</i>

00:04:43.130 --> 00:04:46.770
<i>There's less than a 1% chance for 
me to get a direct hit off Akagi.</i>

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:50.060
<i>And waiting to get a tsumo with</i>

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:53.510
<i>an equally small chance 
isn't getting me anywhere.</i>

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:56.830
<i>Both their hands are still 
far from being ready.</i>

00:04:56.830 --> 00:05:01.190
<i>This huge hand should be 
bagged sooner than later.</i>

00:05:01.190 --> 00:05:02.880
<i>That is logical.</i>

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:06.810
<i>But, Suzuki, that's precisely the 
reason that we'll keep going.</i>

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:09.130
<i>Deliberately keep playing.</i>

00:05:09.130 --> 00:05:13.550
<i>Keep playing and stalk him.</i>

00:05:13.550 --> 00:05:15.660
<i>Something's not right 
in that brat's mind.</i>

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:17.800
<i>He's a freak who doesn't fear death.</i>

00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:20.790
<i>In order to kill a lunatic like that,</i>

00:05:20.790 --> 00:05:24.070
<i>we also have to abandon 
that which is normal.</i>

00:05:24.070 --> 00:05:29.690
<i>Only then can we snare 
him and kill him.</i>

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:31.300
<i>Follow him!</i>

00:05:31.300 --> 00:05:31.900
<i>Chase him!</i>

00:05:31.900 --> 00:05:32.520
<i>Stalk him!</i>

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:34.910
<i>Pursue him relentlessly and kill him!</i>

00:05:34.910 --> 00:05:37.690
<i>Right now. Right here!</i>

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:42.880
<i>The ultimate goal is to get a 
tsumo or to get a direct hit.</i>

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:49.480
Suzuki follows Washizu's orders and 
delays dealing into his hand yet again.

00:05:49.940 --> 00:05:53.170
Washizu abandons reason and 
chooses to keep the game going.

00:05:56.910 --> 00:05:58.490
On the other hand, Akagi...

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:01.600
draws an effective tile.

00:06:02.170 --> 00:06:04.240
He has now drawn five 
effective tiles in a row.

00:06:07.710 --> 00:06:09.740
Despite that, he's still two tiles from tenpai.

00:06:10.330 --> 00:06:12.740
The way to victory is still long.

00:06:12.740 --> 00:06:15.990
In that sense, 
Washizu had inferred correctly.

00:06:17.290 --> 00:06:21.250
Akagi was still far from the 
goal, so he had time to spare.

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:26.250
However, it only seems 
that way at first glance.

00:06:27.230 --> 00:06:30.400
Once a certain condition
is met, Akagi's hand

00:06:30.400 --> 00:06:32.510
will progress at breakneck speed.

00:06:33.310 --> 00:06:35.200
Washizu was underestimating this.

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:40.470
This change, this shifting that 
happens in Mahjong, and its possibilities.

00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:42.950
And then, Yasuoka...

00:06:45.830 --> 00:06:47.410
draws it.

00:06:47.410 --> 00:06:49.220
The fated 1 of circles.

00:06:49.220 --> 00:06:51.990
The tile that will decide this match

00:06:52.600 --> 00:06:54.350
and the fates of Akagi and Washizu.

00:06:58.960 --> 00:07:00.220
<i>How can this be?!</i>

00:07:00.220 --> 00:07:04.200
<i>Of all the tiles, 
how could he draw that one?!</i>

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:10.260
Washizu's winning tile, the last 
1 of circles, ends up with Yasuoka.

00:07:13.950 --> 00:07:16.520
Washizu no longer has the 
chance to win with a tsumo.

00:07:16.520 --> 00:07:20.460
Now he can only win by 
Suzuki dealing into his hand,

00:07:20.970 --> 00:07:24.420
or by getting a direct hit off Akagi, 
which is 99% unlikely.

00:07:25.590 --> 00:07:27.730
To make matters worse for Washizu,

00:07:27.730 --> 00:07:29.130
with the drawing of this 1 of circles,

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:32.320
the conditions for Akagi's 
side have been met.

00:07:32.990 --> 00:07:36.820
Akagi, who's been quietly 
laying low for so long...

00:07:39.910 --> 00:07:40.640
Pon.

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:42.430
...finally makes his move.

00:07:45.900 --> 00:07:47.030
<i>What?</i>

00:07:48.530 --> 00:07:49.030
Pon!

00:07:51.850 --> 00:07:52.270
Pon.

00:07:55.340 --> 00:07:56.400
<i>Oh, no!</i>

00:07:56.400 --> 00:07:58.170
<i>I can't believe these bastards!</i>

00:07:58.170 --> 00:08:00.980
<i>They're trying to keep me 
from getting another turn!</i>

00:08:00.980 --> 00:08:03.580
<i>They're trying to shut down 
this hand by themselves</i>

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:06.980
<i>without giving me a 
chance to do anything.</i>

00:08:07.710 --> 00:08:08.220
Chi.

00:08:18.420 --> 00:08:19.060
Pon.

00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:25.970
<i>It'll end... it'll be over...</i>

00:08:26.760 --> 00:08:28.620
<i>He'll have a 3, 6 of circles wait.</i>

00:08:28.620 --> 00:08:33.800
<i>He'll get into tenpai and then 
that cop will deal into his hand.</i>

00:08:33.800 --> 00:08:34.870
<i>It'll be over!</i>

00:08:36.080 --> 00:08:41.960
<i>My 12 dora, my counted yakuman, 
my miracle will disappear...</i>

00:08:41.960 --> 00:08:43.530
<i>It'll disappear!</i>

00:08:43.530 --> 00:08:45.990
<i>Everything will be wasted.</i>

00:08:53.600 --> 00:08:56.210
<i>Oh, I see. I get it!</i>

00:08:56.210 --> 00:08:58.830
<i>If he's going for a 3, 6 of circles wait,</i>

00:08:58.830 --> 00:09:01.330
<i>he'll have to get rid of the 1 of circles.</i>

00:09:02.060 --> 00:09:05.940
<i>Meaning it'll come out one step 
before the cop can deal into Akagi's hand.</i>

00:09:05.940 --> 00:09:08.340
<i>My 1 of circles!</i>

00:09:09.270 --> 00:09:10.220
<i>I won!</i>

00:09:10.220 --> 00:09:11.650
<i>I've won by one step.</i>

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:14.950
<i>My determination has defeated Akagi!</i>

00:09:14.950 --> 00:09:17.460
<i>It's true that my abnormal wait,</i>

00:09:17.460 --> 00:09:19.450
<i>my drawing things out, 
has created this opening.</i>

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:24.290
<i>This opening allowed 
them to mount an attack,</i>

00:09:24.290 --> 00:09:28.850
<i>but at the same time it also 
got a shot in on that man.</i>

00:09:28.850 --> 00:09:34.070
<i>It created a crack in 
his calm judgment.</i>

00:09:34.980 --> 00:09:37.370
<i>He probably never thought 
I would delay winning so long</i>

00:09:37.370 --> 00:09:41.070
<i>if I was in the position to do so.</i>

00:09:41.400 --> 00:09:43.330
<i>Once I reached the 
yakuman, there's no point</i>

00:09:43.330 --> 00:09:45.710
<i>in insisting on getting 
a tsumo or a direct hit.</i>

00:09:45.710 --> 00:09:48.550
<i>Winning off Suzuki's tile 
would be sufficient.</i>

00:09:49.640 --> 00:09:53.300
<i>With those 48,000 points I wouldn't 
be able to kill him directly,</i>

00:09:53.300 --> 00:09:54.950
<i>but I could kill him with 
the ranking payments.</i>

00:09:54.950 --> 00:09:59.230
<i>There's no reason to prolong the 
risk and delay winning any further.</i>

00:09:59.230 --> 00:10:03.010
<i>That's where he misread me.</i>

00:10:03.600 --> 00:10:06.990
<i>In other words, he misread 
me for someone who needs</i>

00:10:06.990 --> 00:10:12.240
<i>to kill him right away, this instant!</i>

00:10:16.810 --> 00:10:19.370
<i>And these 12 dora...</i>

00:10:19.370 --> 00:10:25.890
<i>The threat of this dealer's yakuman, 
this monster hand, has mislead him.</i>

00:10:25.890 --> 00:10:30.570
<i>Even if this is still East Hand 2, 
catching up to a dealer yakuman is hard.</i>

00:10:30.570 --> 00:10:35.670
<i>That impatience, that irritation 
is what made him move.</i>

00:10:35.670 --> 00:10:37.530
<i>It'll probably pass...</i>

00:10:37.530 --> 00:10:39.010
<i>It'll probably be fine...</i>

00:10:39.010 --> 00:10:41.110
<i>It shouldn't be a problem...</i>

00:10:41.530 --> 00:10:44.870
<i>He acted with that kind of naïve hope.</i>

00:10:44.870 --> 00:10:48.460
<i>This yakuman has poisoned him.</i>

00:10:48.460 --> 00:10:50.940
<i>It poisoned his heart.</i>

00:10:51.700 --> 00:10:55.270
<i>That's why his heart wavered.</i>

00:10:55.270 --> 00:10:56.290
<i>Towards safety...</i>

00:10:56.290 --> 00:10:58.110
<i>That's why it gave in.</i>

00:10:58.110 --> 00:10:59.880
<i>For that one discard!</i>

00:11:01.850 --> 00:11:03.840
<i>He's lacking a certain readiness.</i>

00:11:03.840 --> 00:11:05.120
<i>They're not awake.</i>

00:11:05.120 --> 00:11:06.120
<i>His awareness.</i>

00:11:06.470 --> 00:11:07.120
<i>His mind.</i>

00:11:07.570 --> 00:11:08.120
<i>His senses.</i>

00:11:08.790 --> 00:11:10.960
<i>That's why he will die.</i>

00:11:10.960 --> 00:11:13.360
<i>He will die because of it.</i>

00:11:17.340 --> 00:11:19.370
<i>Now come!</i>

00:11:19.970 --> 00:11:21.880
<i>Come!</i>

00:11:27.800 --> 00:11:30.050
<i>Now discard it.</i>

00:11:30.420 --> 00:11:31.050
<i>Discard it!</i>

00:11:31.390 --> 00:11:32.280
<i>Discard it!</i>

00:11:32.280 --> 00:11:33.490
<i>Discard it!</i>

00:11:33.490 --> 00:11:35.520
<i>That 1 of circles.</i>

00:11:35.520 --> 00:11:37.820
<i>My 1 of circles.</i>

00:11:42.550 --> 00:11:43.390
<i>What's wrong?</i>

00:11:43.390 --> 00:11:44.030
<i>Discard it.</i>

00:11:45.040 --> 00:11:46.670
<i>What's wrong?</i>

00:11:46.670 --> 00:11:48.400
<i>D-Don't tell me...</i>

00:11:48.400 --> 00:11:52.220
<i>You've come all this way, 
and then in the last crucial moment,</i>

00:11:52.220 --> 00:11:54.960
<i>you instinctively sensed the danger,</i>

00:11:56.310 --> 00:12:00.170
<i>the sinister nature of the 1 of circles,</i>

00:12:00.170 --> 00:12:02.090
<i>and are going to play it safe instead?!</i>

00:12:03.910 --> 00:12:05.500
<i>That's right.</i>

00:12:05.500 --> 00:12:06.140
<i>That's it.</i>

00:12:06.140 --> 00:12:06.910
<i>Come.</i>

00:12:06.910 --> 00:12:07.660
<i>Discard it.</i>

00:12:07.660 --> 00:12:09.150
<i>Discard it and be relieved.</i>

00:12:10.120 --> 00:12:13.150
<i>Deal into my 12-dora hand.</i>

00:12:14.670 --> 00:12:15.390
<i>That's it.</i>

00:12:15.390 --> 00:12:16.620
<i>Keep going.</i>

00:12:17.090 --> 00:12:18.120
<i>Come!</i>

00:12:18.120 --> 00:12:18.680
<i>Come!</i>

00:12:18.680 --> 00:12:20.250
<i>Jump into my arms!</i>

00:12:20.250 --> 00:12:22.510
<i>You tasty, tasty 1 of circles!</i>

00:12:22.510 --> 00:12:24.160
<i>Come!</i>

00:12:24.160 --> 00:12:25.030
<i>Discard it!</i>

00:12:25.030 --> 00:12:25.770
<i>Discard it!</i>

00:12:25.770 --> 00:12:26.500
<i>Discard it!</i>

00:12:26.500 --> 00:12:27.230
<i>Discard it!</i>

00:12:27.230 --> 00:12:27.970
<i>Discard it!</i>

00:12:27.970 --> 00:12:29.440
<i>Discard it!</i>

00:12:36.080 --> 00:12:36.800
<i>Ron!</i>

00:12:36.800 --> 00:12:37.410
<i>Ron!</i>

00:12:37.410 --> 00:12:37.910
<i>Ron!</i>

00:12:37.910 --> 00:12:38.310
<i>Ron!</i>

00:12:38.310 --> 00:12:38.710
<i>Ron!</i>

00:12:38.710 --> 00:12:40.990
<i>Ron!</i>

00:12:48.990 --> 00:12:51.690
The chemicals in Washizu's 
brain rush around.

00:12:52.190 --> 00:12:58.730
Beta-endorphins, tyrosine, enkephalin, 
valine, lysine, leucine, isoleucine.

00:12:58.730 --> 00:12:59.960
I won!

00:12:59.960 --> 00:13:00.970
I won!

00:13:01.400 --> 00:13:03.470
I won!

00:13:10.480 --> 00:13:12.480
<i>I survived!</i>

00:13:18.880 --> 00:13:21.420
...hear, Washizu Iwao?

00:13:24.670 --> 00:13:27.460
You didn't hear, Washizu Iwao?

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:32.930
Ron.

00:13:32.930 --> 00:13:34.100
Red dragon, one dora.

00:13:34.100 --> 00:13:35.630
Head bump.

00:13:51.110 --> 00:13:52.590
Stop it!

00:13:53.700 --> 00:13:56.210
Washizu-sama, please stop!

00:13:55.470 --> 00:13:56.380
Washizu-sama!

00:13:56.380 --> 00:13:58.120
Washizu-sama!

00:14:07.950 --> 00:14:10.870
Your senses have dulled, 
Washizu Iwao.

00:14:12.850 --> 00:14:15.600
That's because you are afraid.

00:14:16.660 --> 00:14:17.710
What?

00:14:21.180 --> 00:14:22.050
Impossible!

00:14:22.050 --> 00:14:24.950
Me, afraid?

00:14:24.950 --> 00:14:26.350
That's right.

00:14:27.130 --> 00:14:29.920
That dead wall draw after 
you got to 12 dora...

00:14:30.590 --> 00:14:35.310
That was the crossroads, 
and not just in hindsight.

00:14:35.970 --> 00:14:37.660
You should have realized it then,

00:14:40.180 --> 00:14:44.170
that the flow of the game had been 
reversed and was going against you.

00:14:44.920 --> 00:14:46.490
Instead of chasing me further,

00:14:46.490 --> 00:14:50.100
you should have just let 
Suzuki deal into your hand.

00:14:50.700 --> 00:14:54.940
Then you would have been able to 
at least pick up the 48,000 points.

00:14:56.330 --> 00:14:58.530
You should have been 
satisfied with that.

00:15:00.490 --> 00:15:05.390
But you forced the game onward, 
and dug your own grave.

00:15:07.230 --> 00:15:10.310
Even though it sent you a sign 
that you had reached the limit.

00:15:12.830 --> 00:15:16.830
You ignored that valuable 
warning, that counsel.

00:15:17.580 --> 00:15:18.930
Crude.

00:15:18.930 --> 00:15:19.740
Dense.

00:15:20.460 --> 00:15:22.670
Your regular self probably 
wouldn't have done that.

00:15:23.800 --> 00:15:25.670
Normally you would have listened.

00:15:26.670 --> 00:15:31.180
You would have felt the fine gravity 
of that sign and would have obeyed it.

00:15:32.750 --> 00:15:34.680
You would have made Suzuki 
deal into your hand.

00:15:35.710 --> 00:15:37.380
You would have been reluctant,

00:15:37.380 --> 00:15:39.310
but there wouldn't 
have been any problems.

00:15:40.250 --> 00:15:43.840
But it only looked like you 
had momentum on the surface,

00:15:43.840 --> 00:15:47.630
while deep down in the core of 
your being, you were afraid.

00:15:48.260 --> 00:15:50.260
Because of that,

00:15:50.260 --> 00:15:53.270
your greed took over and insisted 
on getting the tsumo or direct hit.

00:15:55.160 --> 00:15:58.500
Thus you tried to take the 
shortcut to finish the match.

00:15:58.500 --> 00:15:59.670
Preposterous!

00:15:59.670 --> 00:16:00.990
What are you talking about?!

00:16:00.990 --> 00:16:04.510
There's none of that fear in me!

00:16:04.510 --> 00:16:06.030
Not a single ounce of it!

00:16:08.510 --> 00:16:09.250
But...

00:16:09.670 --> 00:16:12.990
I might indeed have 
been caught up in it...

00:16:13.720 --> 00:16:17.990
In the temptation of that 
murderous intent to kill you.

00:16:17.990 --> 00:16:21.360
If I regret anything, it's that.

00:16:21.900 --> 00:16:26.830
I have to weaken it... this intent, 
this temptation to kill you.

00:16:27.320 --> 00:16:27.970
Hey!

00:16:28.350 --> 00:16:28.970
Yes?!

00:16:29.280 --> 00:16:31.500
Pick up the tiles already!

00:16:31.500 --> 00:16:32.700
Yes, sir!

00:16:45.250 --> 00:16:46.880
We're resuming the game!

00:16:49.150 --> 00:16:52.220
Washizu Mahjong resumes 
with East Hand 3.

00:17:03.310 --> 00:17:08.770
<i>Washizu, the real problem is where 
that murderous intent stems from.</i>

00:17:10.650 --> 00:17:13.690
<i>You should have an inkling, as well.</i>

00:17:13.690 --> 00:17:16.250
<i>About where it's coming from.</i>

00:17:16.740 --> 00:17:19.150
<i>Yes, the root of that 
murderous intent...</i>

00:17:20.820 --> 00:17:22.400
<i>is fear.</i>

00:17:23.330 --> 00:17:25.330
<i>You want to kill because 
you don't want to die.</i>

00:17:25.900 --> 00:17:28.800
<i>That's why you rush to kill.</i>

00:17:31.260 --> 00:17:36.300
<i>I got some glimpses of that fear 
in the first and second match, too,</i>

00:17:36.730 --> 00:17:40.300
<i>but this time I was able to 
clearly see it out in the open.</i>

00:17:41.680 --> 00:17:45.310
<i>At the beginning of the third match, 
I could sense this enthusiasm,</i>

00:17:45.310 --> 00:17:51.480
<i>this motivation in Washizu to win 
purely by skill, by outranking me.</i>

00:17:52.990 --> 00:17:57.490
<i>But that feeling was shoved aside 
whenever a chance came to him.</i>

00:17:59.460 --> 00:18:00.980
<i>It was quickly forgotten.</i>

00:18:01.730 --> 00:18:02.800
<i>He wanted to kill.</i>

00:18:02.800 --> 00:18:04.490
<i>He wanted to kill right away.</i>

00:18:05.070 --> 00:18:07.080
<i>He wanted to kill right now.</i>

00:18:07.080 --> 00:18:08.860
<i>He couldn't restrain that impulse.</i>

00:18:09.910 --> 00:18:12.430
<i>Because he wanted to survive himself.</i>

00:18:15.930 --> 00:18:18.910
<i>Yes, that is Washizu's source.</i>

00:18:19.810 --> 00:18:20.910
<i>His desire to live.</i>

00:18:22.730 --> 00:18:25.420
<i>Washizu has an abnormally 
tenacious desire to live.</i>

00:18:26.090 --> 00:18:30.240
<i>After all, his life was driven 
by this most basic fear.</i>

00:18:32.370 --> 00:18:33.920
<i>That's why he wanted to get away.</i>

00:18:34.690 --> 00:18:38.890
<i>He wanted to get as far as possible from 
this fear of death, from destruction.</i>

00:18:40.890 --> 00:18:43.170
<i>In order to achieve that, he had to build.</i>

00:18:43.880 --> 00:18:45.900
<i>More and more.</i>

00:18:47.340 --> 00:18:50.180
<i>In reality, that's all Washizu is.</i>

00:18:53.950 --> 00:18:57.350
<i>The big air he puts on 
and his appearance</i>

00:18:57.350 --> 00:18:59.160
<i>are all because of his money.</i>

00:19:00.590 --> 00:19:06.530
<i>If you remove that costume of 
money, there's isn't much left.</i>

00:19:07.350 --> 00:19:09.190
<i>The thing you'll find there is...</i>

00:19:10.600 --> 00:19:11.990
<i>...a crazed rat.</i>

00:19:13.370 --> 00:19:18.500
<i>A lone, ugly rat with a 
bizarre glint in its eyes.</i>

00:19:20.570 --> 00:19:21.230
Pon.

00:19:26.830 --> 00:19:30.380
<i>Since he discarded the 3 of circles 
after calling the honor tile,</i>

00:19:30.380 --> 00:19:32.310
<i>he's probably in tenpai.</i>

00:19:32.310 --> 00:19:33.110
<i>Damn it.</i>

00:19:36.330 --> 00:19:37.070
<i>There it is.</i>

00:19:37.070 --> 00:19:38.260
<i>I'm in tenpai, too!</i>

00:19:38.260 --> 00:19:40.660
<i>That's if I discard either the 5 
of bamboo or the 3 of characters.</i>

00:19:41.260 --> 00:19:48.630
<i>But it looks like both of these 
are potentially his winning tile.</i>

00:19:48.630 --> 00:19:50.960
<i>Damn!</i>

00:19:52.360 --> 00:19:53.900
<i>I've got no choice.</i>

00:19:53.900 --> 00:19:56.890
<i>I'll play it safe and change my plans.</i>

00:19:56.890 --> 00:19:58.640
<i>I'll go for a chiitoitsu.</i>

00:19:58.640 --> 00:20:01.740
<i>Then I won't have to discard either 
the 5 of bamboo or the 3 of characters.</i>

00:20:03.570 --> 00:20:04.270
Ron.

00:20:09.480 --> 00:20:10.350
What?

00:20:15.030 --> 00:20:18.960
You're actually quite the
coward, Washizu Iwao.

00:20:21.340 --> 00:20:22.290
Me?

00:20:22.770 --> 00:20:25.700
You call me a coward?!

00:20:27.820 --> 00:20:30.200
You can't erase your fear that easily.

00:20:31.140 --> 00:20:33.840
Once your heart has been 
infiltrated by fear,

00:20:33.840 --> 00:20:38.210
you can't break free from being 
weak-spirited that easily.

00:20:39.480 --> 00:20:41.210
So then all I have to do is target...

00:20:43.640 --> 00:20:45.120
those weak spots.

00:20:49.890 --> 00:20:53.140
Akagi has made a recovery 
from his desperate situation.

00:20:53.140 --> 00:20:57.190
Will he be able to push Washizu 
all the way to destruction now?

00:20:58.280 --> 00:21:01.160
The endless battle with death 
and destruction on the line

00:21:01.160 --> 00:21:05.430
is about to enter a stage 
beyond imagination.

00:22:16.260 --> 00:22:19.070
Next time, "Madness and Darkness and..."

00:22:16.880 --> 00:22:20.550
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:22:16.880 --> 00:22:20.550
<b>Madness and Darkness and...</b>
